A Guide to the Solidification of Steels — Jernkontoret (@metal-solidification-guide: 0, is #reference, #part-of @metal-sources) { r_37E0W03MBAM4KMY33EF8BMT9WM
Jernkontoret, Sweden. A Guide to the Solidification of Steels. [Complete four-part authorized educational edition and contents](https://www.phase-trans.msm.cam.ac.uk/2007/Solidification/solidification.html).

Read all four parts: experimental techniques; carbon/low-alloy, chromium, stainless/heat-resistant, and high-speed steel cases; conclusions, references, and alloy index. Compare structures with actual composition, thermal history, observation method, and uncertainty. Preserve the original book/part dates; the host directory does not itself date every experiment.

The author-associated host explicitly states educational reproduction with Jernkontoret's permission. This is not presented as a general adaptation licence. Identity, complete topic outline, four-part access, and permission account were verified on 29 October 2026. The book, micrographs, and external observations are not copied into this repository.

